<title>UK: UK M4 up provisional s/a 11.6 pct yr/yr in June.</title>
<headline>UK M4 up provisional s/a 11.6 pct yr/yr in June.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said on Friday M4 money supply rose a seasonally adjusted 0.9 percent in June for year on year growth of 11.6 percent.  </p>
<p>    MONEY SUPPLY (%)		June		May</p>
<p>    M4 in month   (adjusted)    0.9		 1.4</p>
<p>	 in year to date	    11.6*	    11.1</p>
<p>    M4 in month (unadjusted)    1.2		 2.0</p>
<p>   in year to date		  11.5	     11.3</p>
<p>Adjusted lending by banks,</p>
<p>    b/societies in blns of stg  5.5		 9.1</p>
<p>NOTE - consensus forecast was for 1.0 percent M4 growth on the month for year-on-year growth of 11.1 percent.  </p>
<p>* The annual adusted M4 rate was last higher in December 1990 when it was 12.2 percent.</p>
<p>In June the change in gilt repos included in the change in M4 was -4.2 billion stg, the Bank said. The change in reverse repos included in sterling lending to the M4 private sector was -0.6 billion.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom + 44 171 542 7715</p>
